signed node1's ed25519 host public key into /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals node1, 10.100.43.10, 10y validity), and configured sshd via HostCertificate directive. Verified a client trusting only the CA's public key (via an @cert-authority known_hosts line, no pinned host key) connects successfully under StrictHostKeyChecking=yes, with sshd debug output showing 'matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate'. Falsified by showing the same client fails with an empty known_hosts. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id, triggered `shutdown -r now`, polled until SSH returned, confirmed boot_id changed, and re-verified sshd active, the host certificate still served, and CA-trust-only connection still succeeding post-reboot. Cleaned up all temporary test artifacts (test known_hosts files, temporary SSH keypair, appended authorized_keys entry) added purely for verification.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 SSH config and host keys (OpenSSH 7.2p2 on Ubuntu 16)\",\"Captured baseline: sshd active, listening on :22\",\"Created SSH CA keypair /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca(.pub) via ssh-keygen\",\"Signed node1's ed25519 host public key with the CA producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub with principals node1 and 10.100.43.10, 3650-day validity\",\"Backed up sshd_config and added 'HostCertificate /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub' directive\",\"Validated config with sshd -t and restarted ssh service\",\"Set up a temporary local SSH client trust test using @cert-authority known_hosts entry (no host key pinning) and confirmed successful StrictHostKeyChecking=yes connection\",\"Verified via ssh -vvv debug output that the server presented the ed25519-cert and the client validated it via certificate, not a pinned key\",\"Falsified by connecting with an empty known_hosts file and confirming failure (Host key verification failed)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id from /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id\",\"Triggered a safe reboot via 'shutdown -r now' backgrounded so acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset, proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart: sshd active, host certificate file and sshd_config directive intact, and CA-trust-only client connection still succeeds\",\"Cleaned up all temporary verification artifacts: known_hosts test files, temporary SSH keypair, and the appended authorized_keys line, leaving the pre-existing exec-access key untouched\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"SSH CA created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7588349b3cab4c54\"],\"summary\":\"ssh-keygen generated CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca(.pub)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Host key signed by the CA into a certificate\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2b660903d6fd4691\",\"cmd-e8b9a2e853c249f8\"],\"summary\":\"ssh-keygen -s signed ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub; ssh-keygen -L shows Signing CA, principals node1/10.100.43.10, validity\"},{\"requirement\":\"sshd configured to present the certificate\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-330dc402760643cc\",\"cmd-d4d8c82ec619448e\",\"cmd-8077ae8f68194312\"],\"summary\":\"Added HostCertificate directive to sshd_config, validated with sshd -t, restarted ssh service successfully\"},{\"requirement\":\"Client connects trusting only the CA, without pinning the host key\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1f00110666664020\",\"cmd-aeb6d3999d724445\"],\"summary\":\"SSH connection with only an @cert-authority known_hosts line (no pinned key) succeeded under StrictHostKeyChecking=yes; verbose log shows 'matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate'\"},{\"requirement\":\"Falsification: connection fails without CA trust\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-864d34a540cf47bc\"],\"summary\":\"Same client with empty known_hosts fails strict host key checking, proving the CA trust line (not incidental config) enables the connection\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline healthy state before restar